{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Shall we bring forth water for you from this rock?</b> — Far be it, far be it that the interrogative form should be for negation, for Moses our teacher, who is faithful in all the house of HaShem, nothing from HaShem is too wondrous for him. He and all Israel with him saw greater and more wondrous things than this, and moreover he is the one through whose hand such a thing was once done before, at the rock in Horeb. The commentators have said that there are rhetorical questions that stand as such, like \"Was I revealed?\" (I Samuel 2:27), \"Do you see?\" (II Samuel 15:27), \"Will you judge?\" (Ezekiel 22:2), \"From the tree regarding which I commanded you?\" (Genesis 3:11). But R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] wrote: \"הֲמִן הַסֶּלַע — do we have the power to bring forth water for you from it?\" He intends to explain that Moses said to them: Hear now, you rebels against HaShem, who say \"Why have you brought the assembly of HaShem to this evil place\" — do we have power in nature to bring forth water from this flint? Rather, recognize that it is from HaShem, for He is the one who brought you out of Egypt and brought you to this place, and He is the one who will sustain you in it. This is like the meaning of what He said to them concerning the manna: \"And you shall know that HaShem brought you out of the land of Egypt\" (Exodus 16:6).\n\nBut in my opinion this הוא of interrogation is for a question — \"הֲמִן הַסֶּלַע הַזֶּה נוֹצִיא לָכֶם מַיִם אִם לֹא\" — for Scripture sometimes states both the positive and the negative in a question: \"Is there a tree in it or not?\" (Numbers 13:20), \"Will you keep His commandments or not\" (Deuteronomy 8:2); and sometimes it mentions only the positive: \"Is this your youngest brother?\" (Genesis 43:29), \"Do you know Laban the son of Nahor?\" (Genesis 29:5), \"Should I weep in the fifth month, separating myself?\" (Zechariah 7:3).\n\nBut this question was for them a question of testing. He said: Hear now, you rebels — what do you think of HaShem? Shall we bring forth water for you from this hard rock? Will this thing be or not? He spoke harshly about the rebels and declared that they are of little faith, and when they contend against him it is because of their thinking that HaShem will not perform a wonder for them, as it says: \"And they tested El in their heart… Can El prepare a table in the wilderness? Can He also give bread?\" (Psalms 78:18–20). And so they said (Avot 5:4): Our fathers tested the Holy One, blessed be He, with ten tests in the wilderness.\n\nThis is like the question framed according to the intention of the questioner in many places: \"Shall I return your son?\" (Genesis 24:5) — if such is your desire; \"Shall I go to Ramoth-gilead, or shall I refrain?\" (II Chronicles 18:5) — if such is your counsel; so too here — if your thought is that we shall bring forth water for you from this.\n\nSo too is my opinion regarding \"Was I revealed?\" — \"Have you seen that Ahab has humbled himself before Me?\" (I Kings 21:29) — \"From the tree regarding which I commanded you\" — \"Will you judge?\" — for they are all questions, but their matter is to question about something well-known, which the one questioned is forced to acknowledge: If I revealed myself to your father's house and chose you — if you know this, why do you spurn my sacrifice and my meal-offering? Is this the recompense you repay HaShem? And likewise: If from the tree regarding which I commanded you, you ate and were ashamed and hid — why do you hide? And the rest are in this manner.\n\nBut \"הֲרוֹאֶה אַתָּה\" is a complete question regarding a doubtful matter — \"If you are a counselor, return to the city,\" like the expression \"I see the words of Edom\" (Ketuvot 108b).\n\nAnd I have already explained this in the portion of Genesis (1:4)."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Ibn Ezra as ר״א; resolved as R. Abraham Ibn Ezra per convention. The closing cross-reference is to his commentary on Genesis 1:4."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:20.569805424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}